---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
---

<Layout title="A little studio, a lot of you">
  <article class="content-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">MEET AHAB</p>
    <h1>
      A little studio.
      <br />A lot of you.
    </h1>
    <p>
      Ahab is for people with something to say and no production team on
      standby. A small business owner introducing a product. A creator testing a
      different opening. Someone making their first professional-looking video.
    </p>
    <h2>Start with something personal</h2>
    <p>
      Bring a portrait and your own words. Choose an AI voice or upload your
      narration, then direct a presenter video. If a short visual moment is more
      useful, switch to scene mode and guide it with images and references.
    </p>
    <h2>Approve the words before the take</h2>
    <p>
      Your script remains yours. Ahab adds technical instructions to help the
      video model follow your choices, but your saved prompt history contains
      the words you entered. Check your script, timing and references before
      using a generation.
    </p>
    <h2>A simple creative budget</h2>
    <p>
      Buy a one-time package when you have a project in mind. A finished video
      consumes one allowance. There is no monthly subscription and unused
      allowances do not expire.
    </p>
    <h2>Keep what matters</h2>
    <p>
      Your library has clear storage limits. Older uploads are removed first as
      you add new ones. Generated videos also expire after 121 days. Download
      your finished work to keep it for longer.
    </p>
    <div class="notice">
      <Icon name="info" />
      <p>
        AI presenters and scenes are generated media. Use them honestly, get
        permission to use someone’s likeness, and review the disclosure rules of
        the platform where you publish.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="button-row" style="margin-top:30px">
      <a href="/signup" class="button primary">
        Start creating <Icon name="arrow" size={17} />
      </a>
      <a href="/pricing" class="button secondary">
        See the pricing
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
